  "instruction": "Convert the latest user request into one or two tasks. Resolve people and references using the whole conversation. Do not answer any task. Return only JSON: {\"tasks\": [TASK, ...]}.\nAvailable capabilities and their exact TASK schemas:\n1. directory: records about people in the fictional Luma directory. Schema {\"expert\":\"directory\",\"name\":\"Full Name\",\"field\":\"city\"}. The field must be city, profession, instrument, or hobby. Always write the explicit full name from the conversation, including for the second task. Never use pronouns as names.\n2. protocol: facts about NeuroShard 0.4.0, its client, installation, environment checks, signatures and network. Schema {\"expert\":\"protocol\",\"question\":\"question\"}. Its scope is automatically attached to each protocol question.\n3. parent: general questions outside these specialists. Schema {\"expert\":\"parent\",\"question\":\"standalone question\"}.\nUse a separate task for each requested fact. Never invent a person's name or a new capability. Preserve what the user asked. Do not output explanations or markdown.",
